%% @kicker Exact identifiers
%% @alt A query for error code E-4048 goes to vector search, which returns both E-4048 and the near-identical E-4049 as close matches. A cross-encoder then reads the query and each document together: it rejects the document about E-4049 and keeps the document about E-4048.
%% @caption The textbook case for exact identifiers. The run on this page had the bi-encoder put E-4048 first already, and the larger cross-encoder is what pushed E-4049 well below it.
%% @path query>vec>rerank>exact
%% @glyph query | doc question
%% @glyph vec | vectors
%% @glyph rerank | pair
%% @glyph near | doc cross
%% @glyph exact | doc check
%% @spacing 28,48
flowchart LR
  query["E-4048"]:::accent
  vec["Vector search"]
  rerank["Cross-encoder"]:::focal
  near["E-4049"]:::muted
  exact["E-4048"]
  query --> vec
  vec --> rerank
  rerank -->|no| near
  rerank -->|yes| exact
